---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About — Orbital Notes">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About Orbital Notes</h1>
    <p>
      <strong>Orbital Notes</strong> is a small personal blog about space and orbital
      mechanics, written for the curious — not the credentialed. Every post assumes
      <em>zero</em> prior knowledge of physics or the space domain and builds gently on the
      one before it.
    </p>
    <p>
      What makes these posts different is that the explanations are <em>interactive</em>.
      Instead of staring at a static diagram, you can drag a slider and watch a satellite
      crash, orbit, or escape in real time. The interactive bits are React components
      embedded directly inside the writing, hydrated only when you scroll to them.
    </p>
    <h2>How it's built</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Astro 5</strong> with content collections for the posts.</li>
      <li><strong>MDX</strong> so posts can embed live components.</li>
      <li><strong>React 19 islands</strong>, hydrated with <code>client:visible</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Tailwind v4</strong> via the Vite plugin for styling.</li>
      <li><strong>Motion</strong> for entrance animations.</li>
      <li><strong>KaTeX</strong> (remark-math + rehype-katex) for the equations.</li>
      <li><strong>Recharts</strong> for the charts.</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
